      "id": "nd0uauf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Climate of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's climate is defined as Tropical Monsoon, heavily governed by relief, altitude, pressure belts, and distance from the sea.",
        "The South-West Monsoon advances in two major branches: the Arabian Sea branch and the Bay of Bengal branch.",
        "Pre-monsoon local winds such as Loo, Mango Showers, and Norwesters play a distinct role in seasonal climatic changes.",
        "Global atmospheric phenomena like El Niño weaken monsoon precipitation in India, while La Niña enhances rainfall."
      ],
      "id": "qb51pou"
    },
