      "id": "29ia0po",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. El Niño and La Niña Effect"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Pre-monsoon showers in Kerala and Karnataka are termed 'Mango Showers' (aiding mango ripening) and 'Blossom Showers' (crucial for coffee crops).",
        "The Arabian Sea branch causes heavy orographic rainfall on the windward side of the Western Ghats, leaving the eastern side in rain-shadow.",
        "El Niño causes monsoon rainfall deficit in India, whereas La Niña leads to normal or above-normal rainfall."
      ],
      "id": "kxvtmun"
    },
